    // (languages/lib/kotlin-rt.metajs) / kRecvProps (kotlin-interpreter.abnf): the
    // names that are a PROPERTY of a builtin receiver rather than a zero-argument
    // METHOD of it. The distinction is the whole of it - `with(list) { size }` is a
    // field read and `with(list) { first() }` is a call, and the SAME table decides
    // both in all three engines, so this lowering has to consult it too or the two
    // arms swap. Keep the four lists in step.
