    // ----- Double / Float: a boxed js_jflo value (see abnf/jsrtjvm.go) -----
    // Kotlin's Double is a DIFFERENT type from Int, and the handle runtime models
    // every number as one JS double, so 1.0 / 3.0 and 1 / 3 would arrive here as the
    // same two operands. A floating-point literal emits the js_jflo box and the js_jf*
    // operators answer a Double whenever one operand is one (so 2.5 * 1.5 is 3.75,
    // println(1.0) prints "1.0", and Infinity / NaN / -0.0 exist), which is what
    // kotlin-interpreter.abnf's {__flo} box does.
    //
