    // A declaration that is fully ERASED: it parses, contributes nothing to the module,
    // and is NOT a gap (annotation classes and typealiases are metadata / type sugar).
    function makeErased() { return function(b) { return b } }

    // ----- Imports that name a type this program does not contain -----
    // The SIMPLE name each import brings in, and its `as` alias. An import that RESOLVED
    // puts its types into the program, so a name recorded here that is STILL not a
    // program type came from an import this run could not resolve - which only happens
    // under -warn-imports, i.e. after the user has already chosen to continue past the
    // missing import. `class MyApp : Application()` over an unresolvable
    // `import android.app.Application` is exactly that shape, and it is the commonest
    // `super` in a real Android tree.
    //
