    // `for (ch in 'a'..'c')` yields Chars and `for (i in 1..3)` yields Ints out of the
    // same emitted loop (js_char_like is the identity when the bound is not a Char).
    // ----- THE LOOP VARIABLE IS A FRESH BINDING EACH ITERATION -----
    //
    // A closure made inside the body must capture THAT iteration's value:
    // `for (i in 1..3) { fs.add({ i }) }` is "1 2 3" in Kotlin, and `for (w in
