    // target may be an OUTER lambda with forEach / map / a user function in between, and
    // a return VALUE cannot travel through those. Only the lambda whose own label
    // matches absorbs it (lamCatchBody); anything else rethrows, so it keeps travelling
    // outwards. The twin of the __lamret protocol in kotlin-interpreter.abnf.
    function retLamLabel(b, lbl, v) {
